# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Vite + React project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` package to dependencies
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` accordingly

### 2. Modified Files
- **src/main.tsx**: Added Speed Insights initialization
  - Imported `injectSpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights`
  - Called `injectSpeedInsights()` before rendering the React app

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I used the framework-specific instructions for Vite projects:

- For Vite and other non-React frameworks, the documentation recommends using `injectSpeedInsights()` from the base package
- This function injects the Speed Insights tracking script into the application
- Placed the call before React rendering to ensure tracking is initialized early

## Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed
- ✅ No linting errors (no linter configured in project)
- ✅ All changes follow existing code patterns and conventions

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights tracking script will automatically be served at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`
2. Metrics will be collected from user visits
3. View the Speed Insights dashboard in your Vercel project to analyze performance data

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependency
- `src/main.tsx` - Added Speed Insights initialization code
